 OBJECT                           = DATA_SET_INFORMATION
  DATA_SET_NAME                   = "LRO MOON LASER ALTIMETER 4 GDR V1.0"
  DATA_SET_COLLECTION_MEMBER_FLG  = "N"
  DATA_OBJECT_TYPE                = IMAGE
  START_TIME                      = 2009-07-13T17:33:17.246
  STOP_TIME                       = 2015-04-16T15:22:08.887
  DATA_SET_RELEASE_DATE           = 2015-12-15
  PRODUCER_FULL_NAME              = "GREGORY A. NEUMANN"
  DETAILED_CATALOG_FLAG           = "N"
  DATA_SET_TERSE_DESC             = "Resampled (binned), interpolated
                                     altimetry data products from the 2009
                                     Lunar Reconnaissance Orbiter mission."
  CITATION_DESC                   = "Neumann, G.A., 2009 Lunar Orbiter Laser
                                     Altimeter Raw Data Set,
                                     LRO-L-LOLA-4-GDR-V1.0,
                                     NASA Planetary Data System, 2010."
  ABSTRACT_DESC                   = "
    This data set contains gridded data products from the Lunar Orbiter
    Laser Altimeter instrument [SMITHETAL2009]."

  DATA_SET_DESC                   = "
    Data Set Overview
    =================
The LOLA GDR data products consists primarily of raster Digital Elevation
Models formatted as binary images with detached labels. Ancillary gridded
(binned, averaged) datasets consist of sample density, surface albedo,
slope, roughness, geoid height, and 1064-nm surface reflectance.
The detector noise statistics [BARKERETAL2016, SUNETAL2006] also
provide a crude radiometric measurement of surface brightness at 1064 nm.

The GDR products in this data set are images in Equidistant Cylindrical map
projections at resolutions of 4, 16, 64, 128, 256 and 512 pixels per degree,
as appropriate. Maps at a resolution of 1024 pixels per degree were created
as a preliminary effort. These maps will be updated in the future but are 
currently very sparse. Albedo maps are additionally provided at a 10 pixel 
per degree resolution for consistency with LEMELINETAL2015.  Additional 
DEMS that coregister LOLA data with Kaguya's Selene Terrain Camera are 
given in resolutions of 128, 256 and 512 pixels per degree, also in 
Equidistant Cylindrical map projection.  

In addition, Polar Stereographic projected maps with resolutions from 240
down to 5 meters per pixel are included for the North and South polar regions 
of the Moon. Owing to the large size of many of the GDR products, several 
formats and tiling schemes are employed, as described in the Archive SIS. 
JPEG2000 compression is also used with geospatial headers as appropriate for 
the product in question."

  CONFIDENCE_LEVEL_NOTE           = "

    Overview
    ========
    Data are edited and selected before averaging so as to maintain
    good quality. Where necessary, crossover analysis is done prior to
    averaging so as to minimize discrepancies between individual tracks.

    Data Coverage and Quality
    =========================
    Each nominal monthly orbit provides roughly two tracks per degree of
    longitude at the equator. After each month's data are accumulated,
    crossover adjustments are made to minimize the difference in elevation
    between closely registered tracks and to remove along- and across-track
    orbital errors. The resulting dataset provides better geodetic control
    than that from individual tracks. The first release (March 15, 2010)
    does not incorporate these adjustments, and relies on preliminary
    trajectory solutions. Re-release with better precision and increased
    density has been occuring periodically.

    Limitations
    ===========
    Density of observations increases linearly with time. Higher-resolution
    GDR products will be provided when data density provides coverage in a
    majority of pixels of each data product.
    "
 END_OBJECT                       = DATA_SET_INFORMATION

 OBJECT                           = DATA_SET_TARGET
  TARGET_NAME                     = MOON
 END_OBJECT                       = DATA_SET_TARGET

 OBJECT                           = DATA_SET_HOST
